1. Advanced Distributed Systems Theory & Consensus Mechanics
CAP & PACELC Theorems
The evaluation of state consistency and availability in large-scale systems requires rigorous formal models. Eric Brewer's CAP Theorem posits that under an active network partition (P), a distributed system must sacrifice either Consistency (C, defined as linearizability) or Availability (A, defined as non-failing nodes returning a non-error response without guarantee of latest state).

The PACELC theorem extends CAP to represent system trade-offs more accurately during steady-state execution. It dictates that if there is a Partition (P), a system chooses between Availability (A) and Consistency (C); Else (E), even when operating normally without partitions, the system must trade off between Latency (L) and Consistency (C).                  +-----------------------------------+

