Failure Recovery Mechanics
When step $N$ in a Saga fails, the system must reverse the operations completed in steps $1 \dots N-1$ by executing Compensating Transactions in reverse order. Compensating operations must be designed to be fully idempotent and pivot-aware. The point in the saga beyond which a transaction cannot be compensated is defined as the Pivot Transaction.


