Leaseholder Mechanics: In CockroachDB, every range assigns a specific replica as the Leaseholder. Read requests do not require full Raft consensus round-trips if they are served directly by the Leaseholder. The Leaseholder guarantees that it holds the only valid read/write lease for a key range over a specified duration.
Raft Leader Placement: To minimize write latencies, the system can automatically migrate the Raft leader and Leaseholder to the geographic region generating the highest volume of write requests for a given range.


Advanced Sharding Mechanics & Resharding
When relational storage datasets exceed the physical capacity of a single server instance, data must be sharded across independent physical database clusters.
Consistent Hashing with Virtual Nodes
Traditional modulo sharding ($\text{hash}(key) \pmod N$) causes massive data movement when adding or removing database nodes. Consistent hashing places both nodes and keys on a continuous 32-bit logical ring.                  Consistent Hash Ring (0 to 2^32 - 1)

                             [ Node A_vnode1 ]

                                /         \

                         (Keys)          [ Node B_vnode1 ]

                          /                   \

               [ Node C_vnode1 ]              (Keys)

                          \                   /

                         (Keys)          [ Node A_vnode2 ]

                                \         /

                             [ Node B_vnode2 ]

Virtual Nodes (vnodes): To prevent uneven data distributions (hotspots), each physical machine is assigned multiple virtual positions (e.g., 256 vnodes) along the ring.
Data Placement: A key is mapped to the hash ring by hashing its primary key. The key is assigned to the first virtual node encountered when moving clockwise around the ring.
